    "reason": "There are no training checkpoints. The closest analogue is the iteration at which the FBS algorithm returns its solution. Algorithm 1 only says it returns when unspecified 'stopping criteria are met', and the paper does not define tolerance or Niter values. This vague wording is comparable to 'trained to convergence', hence P."
